<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n13257" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">depso</span></b> , sui, stum, 3, v. a., =
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δεψέω</span>, to <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>knead</i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Prop.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">id ubi excoxeris, depsito bene,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 90</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">id. ib. 76</span></i>: lu 
			 tum, <i><span class="en">id. ib. 40, 4</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">coria,</span>”
				<i>to dress, to curry</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 135</span></i>
			: tibi fortasse alius molit et depsit, Varr. ap.
					<i><span class="en">Non. 99,
			14</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, in an obscene sense, <i>to dishonor</i>, acc. to <i><span class="en">Cic. Fam.
				9, 22, 4</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
